{"_id":"6920a8647c7d1fa20e766dbc","roadmapSlug":"backend","nodeId":"utA1W2O6pzoV_LbtDE5DN","description":"# CSS\n\nCSS (Cascading Style Sheets) is a stylesheet language used to describe the presentation of a document written in HTML or XML (including XML dialects such as SVG, MathML or XHTML). It controls the layout, colors, fonts, and other visual aspects of web pages, ensuring a consistent and visually appealing user experience. CSS allows developers to separate content from presentation, making websites easier to maintain and update.","resources":[{"type":"roadmap","title":"Visit the Dedicated CSS Roadmap","url":"https://roadmap.sh/css","_id":"6a7588bab0650226a5eb4484"},{"type":"article","title":"CSS MDN Docs","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/Styling_basics/What_is_CSS","_id":"6a7588bab0650226a5eb4485"},{"type":"video","title":"CSS Tutorial ΓÇô Full Course for Beginners","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OXGznpKZ_sA","_id":"6a7588bab0650226a5eb4486"}],"createdAt":"2025-11-21T17:59:00.224Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T07:26:50.654Z","lessonPacks":[{"_id":"6a22adddac1c5fa9928ab3ab","title":"CSS Fundamentals","slug":"css","description":"Style, lay out, and debug real pages without fighting the cascade.","lessonIds":["6a15d62fac1c5fa9928a3fb6","6a15e1b0ac1c5fa9928a403f","6a16f11aac1c5fa9928a7c14","6a19dcdfac1c5fa9928a84a5","6a19e79cac1c5fa9928a8571","6a19f85cac1c5fa9928a8654","6a1d7a23ac1c5fa9928a8b4e","6a1dd2daac1c5fa9928a9884","6a1ecf18ac1c5fa9928a9a81","6a1f3245ac1c5fa9928a9cdd","6a20aa64ac1c5fa9928aa44a","6a20ba69ac1c5fa9928aa755","6a20c105ac1c5fa9928aa818","6a20c2e5ac1c5fa9928aa847","6a20c490ac1c5fa9928aa871","6a20c5adac1c5fa9928aa884","6a20c6a5ac1c5fa9928aa897","6a20c7c5ac1c5fa9928aa8aa","6a20ca2fac1c5fa9928aa8d0","6a20cb82ac1c5fa9928aa8e3"],"projectIds":["68b7185fffbff9183d772aed","68b7185fffbff9183d772aee","68b7185fffbff9183d772af0","68b7185fffbff9183d772af6","6a26960eac1c5fa9928acb63","6a26b431ac1c5fa9928acefa"],"fe